"DLMF: §22.4 Periods, Poles, and Zeros ‣ Properties ‣ Chapter 22 Jacobian Elliptic Functions (https://dlmf.nist.gov/22.4)\nciteturn1241view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://dlmf.nist.gov/22.4\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 189\nL0: 【0†DLMF】\nL1: \nL2:   * 【1†Index】\nL3:   * 【2†Notations】\nL4:   * [Input][Button: Search]\nL5: \nL6:   * 【3†Help?】\nL7:   * 【4†Citing】\nL8:   * 【5†Customize】\nL9:   * AnnotateUnAnnotate\nL10:   * 【6†About the Project】\nL11: \nL12: 【7†22 Jacobian Elliptic Functions】【8†Properties】【9†22.3 Graphics】【10†22.5 Special Values】\nL13: \nL14: # §22.4 Periods, Poles, and Zeros\nL15: \nL16: ⓘ\nL17: \nL18: Permalink:\nL19:     【11†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.4】\nL20: See also:\nL21:     Annotations for 【12†Ch.22】\nL22: ###### Contents\nL23: \nL24:   1. 【13†§22.4(i) Distribution】\nL25:   2. 【14†§22.4(ii) Graphical Interpretation via Glaisher’s Notation】\nL26:   3. 【15†§22.4(iii) Translation by Half or Quarter Periods】\nL27: ## §22.4(i) Distribution\nL28: \nL29: ⓘ\nL30: Keywords:\nL31:     【16†Jacobian elliptic functions】, 【17†congruent points】, 【18†coperiodic】, 【19†copolar】, 【20†periods】, 【21†poles】, 【22†zeros】\nL32: Notes:\nL33:     See Lawden (【23†1989】, pp. 24–30), Walker (【24†1996】, pp. 126–131), Whittaker and Watson (【25†1927】, pp. 491–498).\nL34: Referenced by:\nL35:     【26†Erratum (V1.0.3) for References】\nL36: Permalink:\nL37:     【27†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.4.i】\nL38: Addition (effective with 1.0.3):\nL39:     The paragraph on the distribution of the $k$-zeros was added.\nL40: See also:\nL41:     Annotations for 【28†§22.4】 and 【12†Ch.22】\nL42: For each Jacobian function, Table 【29†22.4.1】 gives its periods in the $z$-plane in the left column, and the position of one of its poles in the second row. The other poles are at congruent points, which is the set of points obtained by making translations by $2mK+2n\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$, where $m,n\\in \\mathbb{Z}$. For example, the poles of $\\mathrm{sn}(z,k)$, abbreviated as $\\mathrm{sn}$ in the following tables, are at $z=2mK+(2n+1)\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$.\nL43: Table 22.4.1: Periods and poles of Jacobian elliptic functions.\nL44: Periods  | $z$-Poles\nL45: --- | ---\nL46: $\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$  | $K+\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$  | $K$  | $0$\nL47: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL48: $4K$, $2\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$  | $\\mathrm{sn}$  | $\\mathrm{cd}$  | $\\mathrm{dc}$  | $\\mathrm{ns}$\nL49: $4K$, $2K+2\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$  | $\\mathrm{cn}$  | $\\mathrm{sd}$  | $\\mathrm{nc}$  | $\\mathrm{ds}$\nL50: $2K$, $4\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$  | $\\mathrm{dn}$  | $\\mathrm{nd}$  | $\\mathrm{sc}$  | $\\mathrm{cs}$\nL51: \nL52: ⓘ\nL53: Symbols:\nL54:     【30†$\\mathrm{cd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【31†$\\mathrm{cn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【32†$\\mathrm{cs}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【30†$\\mathrm{dc}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【33†$\\mathrm{dn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【34†$\\mathrm{ds}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【31†$\\mathrm{nc}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【33†$\\mathrm{nd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【35†$\\mathrm{ns}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【32†$\\mathrm{sc}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【34†$\\mathrm{sd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【35†$\\mathrm{sn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【36†${K}^{\\prime }\\left(k\\right)$: Legendre’s complementary complete elliptic integral of the first kind】, 【37†$K\\left(k\\right)$: Legendre’s complete elliptic integral of the first kind】, 【38†$\\mathrm{i}$: imaginary unit】 and 【39†$z$: complex】\nL55: A&S Ref:\nL56:     Table 16.2 (modified)\nL57: Referenced by:\nL58:     【40†§22.4(i)】, 【41†§22.4(i)】, 【42†§22.4(i)】\nL59: Permalink:\nL60:     【43†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.4.T1】\nL61: See also:\nL62:     Annotations for 【44†§22.4(i)】, 【28†§22.4】 and 【12†Ch.22】\nL63: Three functions in the same column of Table 【29†22.4.1】 are copolar, and four functions in the same row are coperiodic.\nL64: \nL65: Table 【45†22.4.2】 displays the periods and zeros of the functions in the $z$-plane in a similar manner to Table 【29†22.4.1】. Again, one member of each congruent set of zeros appears in the second row; all others are generated by translations of the form $2mK+2n\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$, where $m,n\\in \\mathbb{Z}$.\nL66: Table 22.4.2: Periods and zeros of Jacobian elliptic functions.\nL67: Periods  | $z$-Zeros\nL68: --- | ---\nL69: $0$  | $K$  | $K+\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$  | $\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$\nL70: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL71: $4K$, $2\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$  | $\\mathrm{sn}$  | $\\mathrm{cd}$  | $\\mathrm{dc}$  | $\\mathrm{ns}$\nL72: $4K$, $2K+2\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$  | $\\mathrm{sd}$  | $\\mathrm{cn}$  | $\\mathrm{ds}$  | $\\mathrm{nc}$\nL73: $2K$, $4\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$  | $\\mathrm{sc}$  | $\\mathrm{cs}$  | $\\mathrm{dn}$  | $\\mathrm{nd}$\nL74: \nL75: ⓘ\nL76: Symbols:\nL77:     【30†$\\mathrm{cd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【31†$\\mathrm{cn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【32†$\\mathrm{cs}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【30†$\\mathrm{dc}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【33†$\\mathrm{dn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【34†$\\mathrm{ds}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【31†$\\mathrm{nc}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【33†$\\mathrm{nd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【35†$\\mathrm{ns}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【32†$\\mathrm{sc}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【34†$\\mathrm{sd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【35†$\\mathrm{sn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【36†${K}^{\\prime }\\left(k\\right)$: Legendre’s complementary complete elliptic integral of the first kind】, 【37†$K\\left(k\\right)$: Legendre’s complete elliptic integral of the first kind】, 【38†$\\mathrm{i}$: imaginary unit】 and 【39†$z$: complex】\nL78: A&S Ref:\nL79:     Table 16.2 (modified)\nL80: Referenced by:\nL81:     【42†§22.4(i)】\nL82: Permalink:\nL83:     【46†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.4.T2】\nL84: See also:\nL85:     Annotations for 【44†§22.4(i)】, 【28†§22.4】 and 【12†Ch.22】\nL86: Figure 【47†22.4.1】 illustrates the locations in the $z$-plane of the poles and zeros of the three principal Jacobian functions in the rectangle with vertices $0$, $2K$, $2K+2\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$, $2\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$. The other poles and zeros are at the congruent points.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDLMF: §22.8 Addition Theorems ‣ Properties ‣ Chapter 22 Jacobian Elliptic Functions (https://dlmf.nist.gov/22.8)\nciteturn1241view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://dlmf.nist.gov/22.8\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 388\nL0: 【0†DLMF】\nL1: \nL2:   * 【1†Index】\nL3:   * 【2†Notations】\nL4:   * [Input][Button: Search]\nL5: \nL6:   * 【3†Help?】\nL7:   * 【4†Citing】\nL8:   * 【5†Customize】\nL9:   * AnnotateUnAnnotate\nL10:   * 【6†About the Project】\nL11: \nL12: 【7†22 Jacobian Elliptic Functions】【8†Properties】【9†22.7 Landen Transformations】【10†22.9 Cyclic Identities】\nL13: \nL14: # §22.8 Addition Theorems\nL15: \nL16: ⓘ\nL17: \nL18: Keywords:\nL19:     【11†Jacobian elliptic functions】, 【12†addition theorems】\nL20: Permalink:\nL21:     【13†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.8】\nL22: See also:\nL23:     Annotations for 【14†Ch.22】\nL24: ###### Contents\nL25: \nL26:   1. 【15†§22.8(i) Sum of Two Arguments】\nL27:   2. 【16†§22.8(ii) Alternative Forms for Sum of Two Arguments】\nL28:   3. 【17†§22.8(iii) Special Relations Between Arguments】\nL29: ## §22.8(i) Sum of Two Arguments\nL30: \nL31: ⓘ\nL32: \nL33: Notes:\nL34:     See Lawden (【18†1989】, pp. 33–36), Walker (【19†1996】, pp. 126–131), Whittaker and Watson (【20†1927】, pp. 494–498).\nL35: Permalink:\nL36:     【21†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.8.i】\nL37: See also:\nL38:     Annotations for 【22†§22.8】 and 【14†Ch.22】\nL39: \nL40: For $u,v\\in ℂ$, and with the common modulus $k$ suppressed:\nL41: 22.8.1  |  | $\\mathrm{sn}(u+v)$  | $={\\displaystyle \\frac{\\mathrm{sn}u\\mathrm{cn}v\\mathrm{dn}v+\\mathrm{sn}v\\mathrm{cn}u\\mathrm{dn}u}{1-{k}^{2}{\\mathrm{sn}}^{2}u{\\mathrm{sn}}^{2}v}},$  |\nL42: ⓘ\nL43: Symbols:\nL44:     【23†$\\mathrm{cn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【24†$\\mathrm{dn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【25†$\\mathrm{sn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【26†$u$: complex】, 【26†$v$: complex】 and 【26†$k$: modulus】\nL45: A&S Ref:\nL46:     16.17.1\nL47: Referenced by:\nL48:     【27†§22.18(iv)】\nL49: Permalink:\nL50:     【28†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.8.E1】\nL51: Encodings:\nL52:     【29†TeX】, 【30†pMML】, 【31†png】\nL53: See also:\nL54:     Annotations for 【32†§22.8(i)】, 【22†§22.8】 and 【14†Ch.22】\nL55: 22.8.2  |  | $\\mathrm{cn}(u+v)$  | $={\\displaystyle \\frac{\\mathrm{cn}u\\mathrm{cn}v-\\mathrm{sn}u\\mathrm{dn}u\\mathrm{sn}v\\mathrm{dn}v}{1-{k}^{2}{\\mathrm{sn}}^{2}u{\\mathrm{sn}}^{2}v}},$  |\nL56: ⓘ\nL57: Symbols:\nL58:     【23†$\\mathrm{cn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【24†$\\mathrm{dn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【25†$\\mathrm{sn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【26†$u$: complex】, 【26†$v$: complex】 and 【26†$k$: modulus】\nL59: A&S Ref:\nL60:     16.17.2\nL61: Referenced by:\nL62:     【33†§22.6(ii)】\nL63: Permalink:\nL64:     【34†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.8.E2】\nL65: Encodings:\nL66:     【35†TeX】, 【36†pMML】, 【37†png】\nL67: See also:\nL68:     Annotations for 【32†§22.8(i)】, 【22†§22.8】 and 【14†Ch.22】\nL69: 22.8.3  |  | $\\mathrm{dn}(u+v)$  | $={\\displaystyle \\frac{\\mathrm{dn}u\\mathrm{dn}v-{k}^{2}\\mathrm{sn}u\\mathrm{cn}u\\mathrm{sn}v\\mathrm{cn}v}{1-{k}^{2}{\\mathrm{sn}}^{2}u{\\mathrm{sn}}^{2}v}}.$  |\nL70: ⓘ\nL71: Symbols:\nL72:     【23†$\\mathrm{cn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【24†$\\mathrm{dn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【25†$\\mathrm{sn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【26†$u$: complex】, 【26†$v$: complex】 and 【26†$k$: modulus】\nL73: A&S Ref:\nL74:     16.17.3\nL75: Permalink:\nL76:     【38†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.8.E3】\nL77: Encodings:\nL78:     【39†TeX】, 【40†pMML】, 【41†png】\nL79: See also:\nL80:     Annotations for 【32†§22.8(i)】, 【22†§22.8】 and 【14†Ch.22】\nL81: 22.8.4  |  | $$\\mathrm{cd}(u+v)=\\frac{\\mathrm{cd}u\\mathrm{cd}v-k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{2}\\mathrm{sd}u\\mathrm{nd}u\\mathrm{sd}v\\mathrm{nd}v}{1+{k}^{2}k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{2}{\\mathrm{sd}}^{2}u{\\mathrm{sd}}^{2}v},$$  |\nL82: ⓘ\nL83: Symbols:\nL84:     【42†$\\mathrm{cd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【24†$\\mathrm{nd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【43†$\\mathrm{sd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【26†$u$: complex】, 【26†$v$: complex】 and 【26†$k$: modulus】\nL85: Permalink:\nL86:     【44†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.8.E4】\nL87: Encodings:\nL88:     【45†TeX】, 【46†pMML】, 【47†png】\nL89: See also:\nL90:     Annotations for 【32†§22.8(i)】, 【22†§22.8】 and 【14†Ch.22】\nL91: 22.8.5  |  | $\\mathrm{sd}(u+v)$  | $={\\displaystyle \\frac{\\mathrm{sd}u\\mathrm{cd}v\\mathrm{nd}v+\\mathrm{sd}v\\mathrm{cd}u\\mathrm{nd}u}{1+{k}^{2}k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{2}{\\mathrm{sd}}^{2}u{\\mathrm{sd}}^{2}v}},$  |\nL92: ⓘ\nL93: Symbols:\nL94:     【42†$\\mathrm{cd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【24†$\\mathrm{nd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【43†$\\mathrm{sd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【26†$u$: complex】, 【26†$v$: complex】 and 【26†$k$: modulus】\nL95: Permalink:\nL96:     【48†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.8.E5】\nL97: Encodings:\nL98:     【49†TeX】, 【50†pMML】, 【51†png】\nL99: See also:\nL100:     Annotations for 【32†§22.8(i)】, 【22†§22.8】 and 【14†Ch.22】\nL101: 22.8.6  |  | $\\mathrm{nd}(u+v)$  | $={\\displaystyle \\frac{\\mathrm{nd}u\\mathrm{nd}v+{k}^{2}\\mathrm{sd}u\\mathrm{cd}u\\mathrm{sd}v\\mathrm{cd}v}{1+{k}^{2}k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{2}{\\mathrm{sd}}^{2}u{\\mathrm{sd}}^{2}v}},$  |\nL102: ⓘ\nL103: Symbols:\nL104:     【42†$\\mathrm{cd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【24†$\\mathrm{nd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【43†$\\mathrm{sd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【26†$u$: complex】, 【26†$v$: complex】 and 【26†$k$: modulus】\nL105: Permalink:\nL106:     【52†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.8.E6】\nL107: Encodings:\nL108:     【53†TeX】, 【54†pMML】, 【55†png】\nL109: See also:\nL110:     Annotations for 【32†§22.8(i)】, 【22†§22.8】 and 【14†Ch.22】\nL111: 22.8.7  |  | $\\mathrm{dc}(u+v)$  | $={\\displaystyle \\frac{\\mathrm{dc}u\\mathrm{dc}v+k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{2}\\mathrm{sc}u\\mathrm{nc}u\\mathrm{sc}v\\mathrm{nc}v}{1-k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{2}{\\mathrm{sc}}^{2}u{\\mathrm{sc}}^{2}v}},$  |\nL112: ⓘ\nL113: Symbols:\nL114:     【42†$\\mathrm{dc}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【23†$\\mathrm{nc}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【56†$\\mathrm{sc}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【26†$u$: complex】, 【26†$v$: complex】 and 【26†$k$: modulus】\nL115: Permalink:\nL116:     【57†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.8.E7】\nL117: Encodings:\nL118:     【58†TeX】, 【59†pMML】, 【60†png】\nL119: See also:\nL120:     Annotations for 【32†§22.8(i)】, 【22†§22.8】 and 【14†Ch.22】\nL121: 22.8.8  |  | $\\mathrm{nc}(u+v)$  | $={\\displaystyle \\frac{\\mathrm{nc}u\\mathrm{nc}v+\\mathrm{sc}u\\mathrm{dc}u\\mathrm{sc}v\\mathrm{dc}v}{1-k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{2}{\\mathrm{sc}}^{2}u{\\mathrm{sc}}^{2}v}},$  |\nL122: ⓘ\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDLMF: §22.9 Cyclic Identities ‣ Properties ‣ Chapter 22 Jacobian Elliptic Functions (https://dlmf.nist.gov/22.9)\nciteturn1241view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://dlmf.nist.gov/22.9\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 413\nL0: 【0†DLMF】\nL1: \nL2:   * 【1†Index】\nL3:   * 【2†Notations】\nL4:   * [Input][Button: Search]\nL5: \nL6:   * 【3†Help?】\nL7:   * 【4†Citing】\nL8:   * 【5†Customize】\nL9:   * AnnotateUnAnnotate\nL10:   * 【6†About the Project】\nL11: \nL12: 【7†22 Jacobian Elliptic Functions】【8†Properties】【9†22.8 Addition Theorems】【10†22.10 Maclaurin Series】\nL13: \nL14: # §22.9 Cyclic Identities\nL15: \nL16: ⓘ\nL17: \nL18: Keywords:\nL19:     【11†Jacobian elliptic functions】, 【12†cyclic identities】\nL20: Referenced by:\nL21:     【13†§22.8(iii)】\nL22: Permalink:\nL23:     【14†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.9】\nL24: See also:\nL25:     Annotations for 【15†Ch.22】\nL26: ###### Contents\nL27: \nL28:   1. 【16†§22.9(i) Notation】\nL29:   2. 【17†§22.9(ii) Typical Identities of Rank 2】\nL30:   3. 【18†§22.9(iii) Typical Identities of Rank 3】\nL31:   4. 【19†§22.9(iv) Typical Identities of Rank 4】\nL32:   5. 【20†§22.9(v) Identities of Higher Rank】\nL33: ## §22.9(i) Notation\nL34: \nL35: ⓘ\nL36: \nL37: Keywords:\nL38:     【11†Jacobian elliptic functions】, 【12†cyclic identities】, 【21†notation】, 【22†points】, 【23†rank】\nL39: Referenced by:\nL40:     【24†Erratum (V1.0.3) for References】\nL41: Permalink:\nL42:     【25†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.9.i】\nL43: Clarification (effective with 1.0.3):\nL44:     The paragraph after (【26†22.9.6】) was revised to state more precisely the definition of rank.\nL45: See also:\nL46:     Annotations for 【27†§22.9】 and 【15†Ch.22】\nL47: The following notation is a generalization of that of Khare and Sukhatme (【28†2002】).\nL48: \nL49: Throughout this subsection $m$ and $p$ are positive integers with $1\\le m\\le p$.\nL50: \nL51: 22.9.1  |  | $${s}_{m,p}^{(2)}=\\mathrm{sn}(z+2{p}^{-1}(m-1)K\\left(k\\right),k),$$  |\nL52: ⓘ\nL53: Symbols:\nL54:     【29†$\\mathrm{sn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【30†$K\\left(k\\right)$: Legendre’s complete elliptic integral of the first kind】, 【31†$z$: complex】, 【32†$k$: modulus】, 【33†$m$: positive integer】, 【33†$p$: positive integer】 and 【33†${s}_{m,p}^{(r)}$: cyclic quantity】\nL55: Permalink:\nL56:     【34†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.9.E1】\nL57: Encodings:\nL58:     【35†TeX】, 【36†pMML】, 【37†png】\nL59: See also:\nL60:     Annotations for 【38†§22.9(i)】, 【27†§22.9】 and 【15†Ch.22】\nL61: 22.9.2  |  | $${c}_{m,p}^{(2)}=\\mathrm{cn}(z+2{p}^{-1}(m-1)K\\left(k\\right),k),$$  |\nL62: ⓘ\nL63: Symbols:\nL64:     【39†$\\mathrm{cn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【30†$K\\left(k\\right)$: Legendre’s complete elliptic integral of the first kind】, 【31†$z$: complex】, 【32†$k$: modulus】, 【33†$m$: positive integer】, 【33†$p$: positive integer】 and 【33†${c}_{m,p}^{(r)}$: cyclic quantity】\nL65: Permalink:\nL66:     【40†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.9.E2】\nL67: Encodings:\nL68:     【41†TeX】, 【42†pMML】, 【43†png】\nL69: See also:\nL70:     Annotations for 【38†§22.9(i)】, 【27†§22.9】 and 【15†Ch.22】\nL71: 22.9.3  |  | $${d}_{m,p}^{(2)}=\\mathrm{dn}(z+2{p}^{-1}(m-1)K\\left(k\\right),k),$$  |\nL72: ⓘ\nL73: Symbols:\nL74:     【44†$\\mathrm{dn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【30†$K\\left(k\\right)$: Legendre’s complete elliptic integral of the first kind】, 【31†$z$: complex】, 【32†$k$: modulus】, 【33†$m$: positive integer】, 【33†$p$: positive integer】 and 【33†${d}_{m,p}^{(r)}$: cyclic quantity】\nL75: Permalink:\nL76:     【45†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.9.E3】\nL77: Encodings:\nL78:     【46†TeX】, 【47†pMML】, 【48†png】\nL79: See also:\nL80:     Annotations for 【38†§22.9(i)】, 【27†§22.9】 and 【15†Ch.22】\nL81: 22.9.4  |  | $${s}_{m,p}^{(4)}=\\mathrm{sn}(z+4{p}^{-1}(m-1)K\\left(k\\right),k),$$  |\nL82: ⓘ\nL83: Symbols:\nL84:     【29†$\\mathrm{sn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【30†$K\\left(k\\right)$: Legendre’s complete elliptic integral of the first kind】, 【31†$z$: complex】, 【32†$k$: modulus】, 【33†$m$: positive integer】, 【33†$p$: positive integer】 and 【33†${s}_{m,p}^{(r)}$: cyclic quantity】\nL85: Permalink:\nL86:     【49†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.9.E4】\nL87: Encodings:\nL88:     【50†TeX】, 【51†pMML】, 【52†png】\nL89: See also:\nL90:     Annotations for 【38†§22.9(i)】, 【27†§22.9】 and 【15†Ch.22】\nL91: 22.9.5  |  | $${c}_{m,p}^{(4)}=\\mathrm{cn}(z+4{p}^{-1}(m-1)K\\left(k\\right),k),$$  |\nL92: ⓘ\nL93: Symbols:\nL94:     【39†$\\mathrm{cn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【30†$K\\left(k\\right)$: Legendre’s complete elliptic integral of the first kind】, 【31†$z$: complex】, 【32†$k$: modulus】, 【33†$m$: positive integer】, 【33†$p$: positive integer】 and 【33†${c}_{m,p}^{(r)}$: cyclic quantity】\nL95: Permalink:\nL96:     【53†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.9.E5】\nL97: Encodings:\nL98:     【54†TeX】, 【55†pMML】, 【56†png】\nL99: See also:\nL100:     Annotations for 【38†§22.9(i)】, 【27†§22.9】 and 【15†Ch.22】\nL101: 22.9.6  |  | $${d}_{m,p}^{(4)}=\\mathrm{dn}(z+4{p}^{-1}(m-1)K\\left(k\\right),k).$$  |\nL102: ⓘ\nL103: Symbols:\nL104:     【44†$\\mathrm{dn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【30†$K\\left(k\\right)$: Legendre’s complete elliptic integral of the first kind】, 【31†$z$: complex】, 【32†$k$: modulus】, 【33†$m$: positive integer】, 【33†$p$: positive integer】 and 【33†${d}_{m,p}^{(r)}$: cyclic quantity】\nL105: Referenced by:\nL106:     【38†§22.9(i)】\nL107: Permalink:\nL108:     【57†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.9.E6】\nL109: Encodings:\nL110:     【58†TeX】, 【59†pMML】, 【60†png】\nL111: See also:\nL112:     Annotations for 【38†§22.9(i)】, 【27†§22.9】 and 【15†Ch.22】\nL113: In the remainder of this section the rank of an identity is the largest number of elliptic function factors in any term of the identity. The value of $p$ determines the number of points in the identity. The argument $z$ is suppressed in the above notation, as all cyclic identities are independent of $z$.\nL114: ## §22.9(ii) Typical Identities of Rank 2\nL115: \nL116: ⓘ\nL117: \nL118: Notes:\nL119:     See Khare and Sukhatme (【28†2002】).\nL120: Referenced by:\nL121:     【61†§22.9(v)】\nL122: Permalink:\nL123:     【62†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.9.ii】\nL124: Correction (effective with 1.0.25):\nL125:     In the sentence just below (【63†22.9.10】), the expression ${s}_{m,2}^{(4)}{s}_{n,2}^{(4)}$ has been corrected to read ${s}_{m,p}^{(4)}{s}_{n,p}^{(4)}$.\nL126: \nL127: Suggested 2019-11-07 by Juan Miguel Nieto\nL128: \nL129: See also:\nL130:     Annotations for 【27†§22.9】 and 【15†Ch.22】\nL131: In this subsection $1\\le m\\le p$ and $1\\le n\\le p$.\nL132: ### Three Points\nL133: \nL134: ⓘ\nL135: \nL136: Keywords:\nL137:     【11†Jacobian elliptic functions】, 【12†cyclic identities】, 【64†simultaneously permuted】\nL138: See also:\nL139:     Annotations for 【65†§22.9(ii)】, 【27†§22.9】 and 【15†Ch.22】\nL140: \nL141: With\nL142: \nL143: 22.9.7  |  | $$\\kappa =\\mathrm{dn}(2K\\left(k\\right)/3,k),$$  |\n"

